m III represents the whole plane ${R}^{2}$  without the origin. But every subspace must contain the origin, so Diagram III is not a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is diagram II only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323707 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124628 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb02b67c-90d9-5baf-b00e-590e9271d89e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets Closed Under Addition and Scalar Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b16ecbe9-c123-5857-9769-f9dac3faf9b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467328} {:answer/id #uuid "f26b27de-130c-507d-93c7-a96ecd84d877" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467329}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b16ecbe9-c123-5857-9769-f9dac3faf9b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467328} :answer-field/id #uuid "71d59c2d-9307-5d0c-ae75-e6fa043a32b8" :answer-field/key "$f(x)\\in S,$ where $f(x)=2x.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468385} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "105b805f-626c-510e-9607-294f6d3052af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467330} {:answer/id #uuid "c645ff3c-1f3e-52e7-a675-1735a28d5139" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467331}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "105b805f-626c-510e-9607-294f6d3052af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467330} :answer-field/id #uuid "15c9c1d7-7c6f-570e-bd49-f923b5d980c6" :answer-field/key "For 