academy-id "q-35663" :question/problem "Let $S$ be the set of all polynomials with real coefficients and whose degree is greater than or equal to $2.$  Which of the following statements are true? \n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's verify the statements one at a time.\n\n- Statement “$f(x)\\in S,$ where $f(x)=2x.$” is false. The set $S$ contains only polynomials whose degree is greater than or equal to $2.$ However, \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{deg}⁡(2x)=1\\ne 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=2x\\notin S.$\n\n- Statement “For every $p(x),q(x)\\in S,$ we have $p(x)+q(x)\\in S.$” is false. There exist functions in $S$ such that their sum is *not* in $S.$ For example, let $p(x)=x+{x}^{2}$ and $q(x)=x-{x}^{2}.$ Notice that both these functions belong to $S$ since $\\operatorname{deg}⁡(p(x))=\\operatorname{deg}⁡(q(x))=2\\ge 2.$ However,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{deg}⁡(p(x)+q(x))=\\operatorname{deg}⁡((x+{x}^{2})+(x-{x}^{2}))=\\operatorname{deg}⁡(2x)=1≱2.\n$$\n\nHence, $p(x)+q(x)\\notin S.$\n\n- Statement “The set is closed under addition” is false. Since statement “For every $p(x),q(x)\\in S,$ we have $p(x)+q(x)\\in S.$” is false, the set is *not* closed under addition.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323771 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054816 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d132801-b9cc-5c0c-a8fa-0c8b840c05bd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets Containing a Given Element"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b95a8c9-ef0a-5052-a30e-f82b7c845cdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467334} {:answer/id #uuid "3273b5a4-d168-5995-b944-97e01461a450" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467335}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b95a8c9-ef0a-5052-a30e-f82b7c845cdc" :answe