/id #uuid "14dd13f1-4b3c-5216-b52c-2fb40b464f25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668665} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cd629cd-a28c-5a36-83e5-f18656e98405" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668910}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5188349b-4c96-553c-a9c2-bb2336ff508e" :question/math-academy-id "q-40799" :question/problem "Which of the following values ​are possible outputs of $f(x)=-{(2)}^{-x}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The range of ${2}^{-x}$ is\n\n$$\n{2}^{-x}>0.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $-1$ yields the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1){(2)}^{-x} & <0 \\\\ -{(2)}^{-x} & <0 \\\\ f(x) & <0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the range is $f(x)<0.$ Thus, of the given values, only $y=-0.5$ is an output of $y=f(x).$\n\nWe can also see that this is true from the graph of the function. The graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/95/95ad3043259402375e7b5822aef88d77027222a3372c2b8ab042d1b54e08666f.png)\n\n \n\nSo, the correct answer is “The number $-0.5$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326929 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119784 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e69a4aee-6e92-598b-99b5-1d830b6dea54" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Correct Statements About a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99c6bb28-f335-5bbd-98ef-7c10debcd116" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438308} {:answer/id #uuid "f443bd43-943d-5991-a1db-7e129b593206" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438309}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f443bd43-943d-5991-a1db-7e129b593206" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438309} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbe78ff6-d1f1-58f5-8add-6b463affc7cc" :answer-field/key "$A$ is lower triangular." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439183} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e07dc0e6-51e2-5ce8-a1b4-44727450bef9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438310} {:answer/id #uuid "cef77811-df7c-59ed-a36f-ed5228a3ebc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438311}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e07dc0e6-51e2-5ce8-a1b4-44727450bef9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438310} :answer-field/id #uuid "371815f8-f16e-5680-9ce5-31f3cff1d9be" :answer-field/key "${A}^{T}-A$ is lower triangular." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439184} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76c420bb-1528-5dc2-9b89-925a5134c93a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438312} {:answer/id #uuid "f06b9547-425a-5254-b4f6-2c95fe1f7d28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76c420bb-1528-5dc2-9b89-925a5134c93a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438312} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ba6e7f7-ddb2-5a5c-9829-6eb52ab534d3" :answer-field/key "$A$ is upper triangular." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439185} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8173f18f-e0a2-5131-82f0-0227fae7e578" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668667} {:answer/id #uuid "61d6633d-f8af-56c4-8766-b44324922bad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668668}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8173f18f-e0a2-5131-82f0-0227fae7e578" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668667} :answer-field/id #uuid "997b143e-f42a-5f22-a792-09b4bfe39e93" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668911}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7fc84187-05b2-57ce-8e48-261250d11c80" :question/math-academy-id "q-42116" :question/problem "Consider the matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- $A$ is lower triangular: **True.** This holds because all the entries above the main diagonal are zeros:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- ${A}^{T}-A$ is lower triangular: **False.** This fails because the result of ${A}^{T}-A$ has non-zero entries above the main diagonal:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}-A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $A$ is upper triangular: **False.** This fails because $A$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe true statements are:\n\n- $A$ is lower triangular."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329633 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115334 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf19e2ee-7c42-58b0-9254-5a44f315288a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Block Diagonal and Block Triangular Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf81b5d0-b61e-5203-bb54-801438d3461d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467500} {:answer/id #uuid "fd171565-81f8-50d3-8a91-05948557c95c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467501}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf81b5d0-b61e-5203-bb54-801438d3461d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467500} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a853d7c-2687-518d-a446-c138652f4c7e" :answer-field/key "$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 8\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468471} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc4d0664-5482-5544-9e91-690f058f2d43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467502} {:answer/id #uuid "12bbe01a-fe98-5ec1-a6c8-24a6cbbe1cca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467503}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc4d0664-5482-5544-9e91-690f058f2d43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467502} :answer-field/id #uuid "34b3dc6c-709b-5dee-acff-ac14c1ddc707" :answer-field/key "$B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468472} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "825129c8-74ee-54bf-8b70-10f615c4071d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467504} {:answer/id #uuid "35dfa222-4364-5bbd-af7c-c6cfea240e47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467505}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "825129c8-74ee-54bf-8b70-10f615c4071d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467504} :answer-field/id #uuid "5535032e-f5c6-5f9b-b4e5-bbd70b524e51" :answer-field/key "$C=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468473} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2391fa3e-1443-5b46-884d-207e7175c4c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668669} {:answer/id #uuid "65ee46e6-2656-5d11-953d-b61edd996c7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668670}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65ee46e6-2656-5d11-953d-b61edd996c7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668670} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7986c7e-ad3f-5069-a12a-54cd3db19300" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668912}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b1e9c127-3ff2-5d29-89f3-9a02b595895a" :question/math-academy-id "q-42138" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are block upper triangular?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A block upper triangular matrix can be partitioned so that it has only square blocks on the main diagonal, and the blocks below the main diagonal contain only zeros.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- $A$ is *not* a block upper triangular matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 8\\end{bmatrix},\\,A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 8\\end{bmatrix},\\,A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $B$ is *not* a block upper triangular matrix since it can't be partitioned in a way described above:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $C$ is *not* a block upper triangular matrix since it can't be partitioned in a way described above:\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329688 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176051 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e2a8cf2-64db-5b2f-b0f7-0c727cf492a9" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Secant Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62c719e0-d25a-59ec-a391-67f41278bccc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467530} {:answer/id #uuid "849fb659-4d9a-5640-b741-4b42c0a2fe08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467531}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62c719e0-d25a-59ec-a391-67f41278bccc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467530} :answer-field/id #uuid "5936cb4f-6ef1-5007-8ddb-e8fa3ea9a73e" :answer-field/key "$x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ is in the domain." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468486} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58ddd5cd-f2b6-5fce-9e50-51af7059d7a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467532} {:answer/id #uuid "4eccff29-5dd8-5062-bdc3-d964a3b204b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58ddd5cd-f2b6-5fce-9e50-51af7059d7a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467532} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3481d3b-57f8-5225-b91c-3c0be05b7ac7" :answer-field/key "$x=\\pi $ is a root." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468487} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a03323e1-ad31-55cd-86ab-f5fa0debeb5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467534} {:answer/id #uuid "926a9028-0022-5d33-98e5-63757d49eabb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467535}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "926a9028-0022-5d33-98e5-63757d49eabb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467535} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c53ddf1-c2d8-545a-bdb3-ed7c844e7094" :answer-field/key "$y=\\frac{1}{2}$ is not in the range of the function." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468488} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc8f1978-fc43-5607-8473-bdd33f26ffc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668671} {:answer/id #uuid "8a8165bc-5b1a-52ca-9b09-edf7f1d512a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668672}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc8f1978-fc43-5607-8473-bdd33f26ffc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668671} :answer-field/id #uuid "abc22e4f-fd1b-5570-b4e4-916e6f9f0e4f" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668913}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "84d0f456-e91d-5ae9-ab2b-9060640f7227" :question/math-academy-id "q-42853" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=sec⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=sec⁡x.$\n\n![](images/da/da729794a0331383debd75be0a4ce4a9f2d4da3286f50bd4f284868996077412.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement “$x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ is in the domain” is false. The function is defined for all real numbers except the values $\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi $ for any integer $n,$ thus it is not defined for $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.$\n\n- Statement “$x=\\pi $ is a root” is false. The function has no zeros.\n\n- Statement “$y=\\frac{1}{2}$ is not in the range of the function” is true. The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ),$ so $y=\\frac{1}{2}$ does not belong to the range."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329692 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176051 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e2a8cf2-64db-5b2f-b0f7-0c727cf492a9" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Secant Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64b39f5b-1a9f-5406-a6a3-ca922728ac21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467536} {:answer/id #uuid "a82257d2-6939-5094-b209-8c3f8a6ca528" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64b39f5b-1a9f-5406-a6a3-ca922728ac21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467536} :answer-field/id #uuid "3aa7fb85-2e34-51b0-801e-44fdce823bfd" :answer-field/key "The point $(0,2)$ is in the graph" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468489} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "334b114b-89c0-5778-85fc-b19d61115037" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467538} {:answer/id #uuid "dcbb6570-b38c-51d8-8e6d-983c8121bded" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467539}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dcbb6570-b38c-51d8-8e6d-983c8121bded" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467539} :answer-field/id #uuid "6155eda5-776d-536c-9839-c334c3fbac7d" :answer-field/key "$x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ is a vertical asymptote" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468490} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46873272-c960-50c8-a66f-af2707c5c86b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467540} {:answer/id #uuid "d2864d48-61db-5ab1-a2bd-c0aa7dc3c175" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467541}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2864d48-61db-5ab1-a2bd-c0aa7dc3c175" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467541} :answer-field/id #uuid "250be72e-dcdb-5259-b3b8-15930933244e" :answer-field/key "$y=-2$ belongs to the range of the function." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468491} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ec9929d-d2a9-5bf0-b0f7-233946a4b462" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668673} {:answer/id #uuid "5b37fac7-f3c0-5557-9a78-6fd1e3f4f6ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668674}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ec9929d-d2a9-5bf0-b0f7-233946a4b462" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668673} :answer-field/id #uuid "55318af8-f00d-5e79-aeb5-16139364f92b" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668914}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3923a242-a394-5f37-9f6d-741dafd435c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-42886" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=sec⁡x.$\n\n![](images/da/da729794a0331383debd75be0a4ce4a9f2d4da3286f50bd4f284868996077412.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement “The point $(0,2)$ is in the graph” is false. The $y$-intercept of $sec⁡x$ is $1.$\n\n- Statement “$x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ is a vertical asymptote” is true. The function $y=sec⁡x$ has asymptotes at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,$ thus $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ is a vertical asymptote.\n\n- Statement “$y=-2$ belongs to the range of the function” is true. The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ),$ so $y=-2$ belongs to the range."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329743 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124628 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb02b67c-90d9-5baf-b00e-590e9271d89e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets Closed Under Addition and Scalar Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba58b671-2657-5a03-abe7-c1d0f53623a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467554} {:answer/id #uuid "ba1c3ce4-672a-5a3c-a83d-bb611ddd59bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467555}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba1c3ce4-672a-5a3c-a83d-bb611ddd59bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467555} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c5d2488-f6b5-5b00-8662-08305a2ef8b5" :answer-field/key "$q(x)\\in W,$ where $q(x)={2}^{x}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468498} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40ba87ba-c6e2-5de6-b649-e0483026a236" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467556} {:answer/id #uuid "62f2e689-0881-5c43-bed6-64a96561cc4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467557}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40ba87ba-c6e2-5de6-b649-e0483026a236" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467556} :answer-field/id #uuid "a50d472b-7d51-5fe0-859e-60a2e6abcfa4" :answer-field/key "For any $f(x)\\in W$ and $k\\in R,$ we have $k\\cdot f(x)\\in W.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468499} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54074d74-4264-5c20-8484-753531648f60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467558} {:answer/id #uuid "e7263bac-9438-5bd2-bceb-9ddd2ae62b91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467559}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54074d74-4264-5c20-8484-753531648f60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467558} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e58aa32-3f2c-58e2-a22d-6bae8ee75a9b" :answer-field/key "The set is closed under scalar multiplication." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468500} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31556811-45d7-55a2-b30e-e33b82a5281c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668675} {:answer/id #uuid "0f1afb21-0ace-5afb-8ae5-76f15e308306" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668676}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31556811-45d7-55a2-b30e-e33b82a5281c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668675} :answer-field/id #uuid "14a9a111-ae72-5c3d-948a-242c5a072a74" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668915}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b4fc2576-da47-56c9-aeca-80fed8de957c" :question/math-academy-id "q-43859" :question/problem "Let $W$ be the set of functions $f:R\\to R$ such that $f(0)=1.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's verify the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement “$q(x)\\in W,$ where $q(x)={2}^{x}.$” is true. Indeed, $q(x)={2}^{x}\\in W$ because\n\n$$\nq(0)={2}^{0}=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement “For any $f(x)\\in W$ and $k\\in R,$ we have $k\\cdot f(x)\\in W.$” is false. There exists a function in $W$ that has a scalar multiple *not* in $W.$ For example, let $f(x)={2}^{x}$ and $k=2.$ Notice that $f(x)$ belongs to $W$ since $f(0)=1.$ However,\n\n$$\n2\\cdot f(0)=2\\cdot {2}^{0}=2\\ne 1.\n$$\n\nHence, $k\\cdot f(x)\\notin W.$\n\n- Statement “The set is closed under scalar multiplication” is false. Since statement “For any $f(x)\\in W$ and $k\\in R,$ we have $k\\cdot f(x)\\in W.$” is false, the set is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$q(x)\\in W,$ where $q(x)={2}^{x}.$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332803 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172082 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd82d96b-34d5-5d20-b810-7ea88b0b5797" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation That Generates a Slope Field Using Stationary Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1400080f-29b9-5c0b-8fff-a02b1e3db551" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467638} {:answer/id #uuid "613a05d1-be2e-50ec-a143-b9bd92523dbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1400080f-29b9-5c0b-8fff-a02b1e3db551" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467638} :answer-field/id #uuid "936bcfa4-d2d6-56bc-951a-d3fb63ec7798" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{y}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468540} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a5309f7-7b7d-5141-8adf-5fd91dcf5b9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467640} {:answer/id #uuid "de6a0b4d-d5db-57b2-b79f-fc23d0c4a768" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467641}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a5309f7-7b7d-5141-8adf-5fd91dcf5b9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467640} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a065266-b7e5-54c1-b994-892844b67807" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}={e}^{y+1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468541} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b3cbfb6-b114-5d0c-bde7-abe9838a454d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467642} {:answer/id #uuid "3503fafc-99d4-55a2-8b84-ae4563b1ad39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467643}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b3cbfb6-b114-5d0c-bde7-abe9838a454d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467642} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbaebdb6-1441-5c65-a2f2-c74e1d11eb4f" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=x(y+1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468542} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e85238a1-af69-5c27-a709-b9ffb1147054" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668677} {:answer/id #uuid "eab7ceb6-127d-5739-8d2c-08d9e25e5a43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668678}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eab7ceb6-127d-5739-8d2c-08d9e25e5a43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668678} :answer-field/id #uuid "451afeed-0ebd-5ade-ba43-f2abc9913049" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668916}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "009c7b44-827f-54c3-aa43-59cb0c58cb71" :question/math-academy-id "q-50143" :question/problem "![](images/50/50472b92dc5fbcc8688bb1d5459f910fb2d3f3c0ee564ba671cb6a53ce8df721.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "![](images/e3/e328914d55b82fdd07147f683aa44aebbc3f3e908f180e6632332119c81ce482.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along the line $y=-1,$ as shown above. Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on this line. \n\nWith that in mind, let's check each equation:\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{y}$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{y}$ is never zero.\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}={e}^{y+1}$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}={e}^{y+1}$ is never zero.\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}=x(y+1)$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=x(y+1)$ evaluates to zero at $x=0$ and $y=-1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of those listed.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332837 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175956 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "60f61c26-ff2d-5343-becd-d8f44f623cd3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Convergence of a Power Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f76e57a-1ca0-528a-83d8-a658b709ba2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467686} {:answer/id #uuid "2bd70b0d-74ff-575c-9f41-331c8052230a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467687}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f76e57a-1ca0-528a-83d8-a658b709ba2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467686} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d9f46eb-7d8b-5c31-85be-40e5cad1c55e" :answer-field/key "The series converges at $x=-3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468564} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5888bd7f-0417-52e2-9a92-7c880ec24bfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467688} {:answer/id #uuid "b848d96c-e2cc-5b77-b15f-3560a9b4590d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467689}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5888bd7f-0417-52e2-9a92-7c880ec24bfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467688} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab3783e8-f88d-556b-acd1-93c5cd956bca" :answer-field/key "The series diverges at $x=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468565} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e011cc9-db9e-52c4-9b70-2cc44c5f65c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467690} {:answer/id #uuid "7816688d-7881-5671-bc85-e7a63dbf447a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467691}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e011cc9-db9e-52c4-9b70-2cc44c5f65c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467690} :answer-field/id #uuid "ccae151c-97cd-5e93-9baa-a5d477ca5334" :answer-field/key "The series converges at $x=8$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468566} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0893ace0-ae6c-5cb0-ad4b-d87606f56d59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668679} {:answer/id #uuid "122a3c03-b162-599c-a675-c19291d8f300" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668680}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "122a3c03-b162-599c-a675-c19291d8f300" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668680} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cadf7f6-1844-5987-80cd-bf023ee2086b" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668917}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0bcb862b-db75-545a-8402-c194bc3da35a" :question/math-academy-id "q-50877" :question/problem "The power series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}(x-3)^{n}$ converges at  $x=-2.$ Which of the following **must** be true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The center of the expansion is $x=3,$ and since the series is convergent for $x=-2,$ this means that the radius of convergence $R$ is *at least* $5,$ i.e., $R\\ge 5.$ So, the series is convergent for every point in the interval $[-2,8).$ However, we know nothing about the convergence of the series at any point outside the interval $[-2,8).$\n\n![](images/38/38763aa0d87065a01ccdf0d94bca2a4e1d6ef227aeab4aaacb9703246eee6abf.png)\n\n \n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of our statements.\n\n- Statement “The series converges at $x=-3$” is false. Since $-3\\notin [-2,8),$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=-3.$\n\n- Statement “The series diverges at $x=1$” is false. Since $1\\in [-2,8),$ the series is convergent at $x=1.$\n\n- Statement “The series converges at $x=8$” is false. Since $8\\notin [-2,8),$  we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=8.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the given statements must be true.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335825 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176053 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92d6129b-a5c5-597a-86ee-3f19af20f326" :knowledge-point/title "Describing the General Properties of the Cosecant Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c29a3814-a545-563e-9080-6c788b49451b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438356} {:answer/id #uuid "d6f89c4d-da0d-58fc-ab37-efc5ed7f1053" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c29a3814-a545-563e-9080-6c788b49451b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438356} :answer-field/id #uuid "30435fb6-1037-57a8-b967-d652cdf699a7" :answer-field/key "The range of the function is all real numbers." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439207} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0ebde88-a46b-560f-9b2d-c9311641fa24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438358} {:answer/id #uuid "d06a8128-c2a1-53e6-bd78-9b4f1b872f74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438359}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d06a8128-c2a1-53e6-bd78-9b4f1b872f74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438359} :answer-field/id #uuid "3aa49081-1dec-5a36-ad7e-37cc67073211" :answer-field/key "$\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2\\pi ).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439208} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70935825-1eb9-59f1-b836-2b74b2e4e965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438360} {:answer/id #uuid "d95548b2-40ec-5ebf-b1ab-d29936ab04f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438361}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70935825-1eb9-59f1-b836-2b74b2e4e965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438360} :answer-field/id #uuid "168eb318-5e34-58b3-8153-3564c073e9ff" :answer-field/key "$x=5\\pi $ is in the domain of the function." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439209} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "adc3a207-169f-5423-80e3-17be47fee7c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668681} {:answer/id #uuid "aad97b35-eab0-5378-b653-222baa5b4bd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668682}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "adc3a207-169f-5423-80e3-17be47fee7c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668681} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e02eeee-fd34-5288-8bf4-c5879a7dd331" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668918}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "69d68c82-75d2-569e-bc5a-a35be8a71a62" :question/math-academy-id "q-65308" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/f1/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ).$ Hence, statement “The range of the function is all real numbers” is false.\n\n- The period of the function is $2\\pi ,$ so $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2n\\pi )$ for any integer $n.$ Substituing $n=1,$ we get $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2\\pi ).$ Hence, Statement $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2\\pi ).$ is true.\n\n- The function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ is defined for all real numbers except the integer multiples of $\\pi ,$ so $5\\pi $ is not in the domain of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$ Hence, statement “$x=5\\pi $ is in the domain of the function” is false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335868 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110588 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7f045b43-4785-5989-8b5a-dcb8401d1bb3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Points that Lie on the Graph of the Inverse Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e29c3cbf-ed0c-5f33-a9f0-4d3cdc0ce3f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467734} {:answer/id #uuid "58f8682f-85e2-5cc2-a2ed-0e7c63277345" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467735}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58f8682f-85e2-5cc2-a2ed-0e7c63277345" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467735} :answer-field/id #uuid "67ac0352-4b5d-55b6-8626-8235d35b0584" :answer-field/key "$(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}},\\frac{\\pi }{6})$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468588} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "543f638b-e58b-5244-baca-fc2e353d3d8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467736} {:answer/id #uuid "10980f56-d3cb-58fa-a676-f80baa5fa827" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467737}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "543f638b-e58b-5244-baca-fc2e353d3d8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467736} :answer-field/id #uuid "2536a64c-f41c-5631-827e-ba3e9fd0aec1" :answer-field/key "$(0,\\frac{\\pi }{4})$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468589} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd154674-e7af-509f-be60-ea578fcd166d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467738} {:answer/id #uuid "15e7fc7a-c51c-56dc-ade0-253f7318ab84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467739}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd154674-e7af-509f-be60-ea578fcd166d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467738} :answer-field/id #uuid "120e82a3-2fc8-5e65-9bb2-4eed01844e71" :answer-field/key "$(-1,\\frac{3\\pi }{4})$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468590} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9dff8055-4afb-5ce9-83a6-35155bb2d35a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668683} {:answer/id #uuid "180ee5ad-febd-5d95-aeef-c0f9baf096b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668684}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9dff8055-4afb-5ce9-83a6-35155bb2d35a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668683} :answer-field/id #uuid "81cf698c-4635-5b28-be41-8e9d7121eab4" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668919}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "abdfc725-c190-5fa3-9b7b-d91b4625d300" :question/math-academy-id "q-65979" :question/problem "Which of the following points lies on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "In order for a point $(a,b)$ to lie on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,$ the following conditions must hold:\n\n- The reflected point $(b,a)$ must lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$\n\n- The $y$-value of the point must lie in the range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,$ which is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of the points. \n\n- First,  we consider the point $(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}},\\frac{\\pi }{6}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\pi }{6},\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and $y=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}},\\frac{\\pi }{6})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$\n\n- Next, we consider the point $(0,\\frac{\\pi }{4}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\pi }{4},0)$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$  $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(0,\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, we consider the point $(-1,\\frac{3\\pi }{4}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{3\\pi }{4},-1)$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and $y=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ does **not** lie within this range. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(-1,\\frac{3\\pi }{4})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335870 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110587 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b834b64-9679-56c2-b5e9-ee26a54b5e13" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Values in the Domain of the Inverse Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c8ce2de-6acd-5eee-a7f7-86b7b0defa87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467746} {:answer/id #uuid "b8a11fe6-7938-5b94-bd6c-0382de6b4167" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467747}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8a11fe6-7938-5b94-bd6c-0382de6b4167" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467747} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ee02da6-8f97-5cd3-b80e-fc016445b3ba" :answer-field/key "$3\\pi $" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468594} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "010b619d-865d-593e-bd64-c95f0b0c0362" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467748} {:answer/id #uuid "774e38d1-2f7d-5c97-bd41-aae4c7260d41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467749}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "774e38d1-2f7d-5c97-bd41-aae4c7260d41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467749} :answer-field/id #uuid "c65441cf-1b51-5ccf-a366-c4f774795164" :answer-field/key "$-\\frac{\\pi }{6}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468595} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cfb632a6-ff6b-54f9-aa91-3eead9fbba45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467750} {:answer/id #uuid "90d5e6d6-781f-545e-9388-772a9903f151" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467751}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90d5e6d6-781f-545e-9388-772a9903f151" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/valu