nswer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8edcd45-9b01-5189-b028-f43c8010f305" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668705} :answer-field/id #uuid "0365a70f-86b6-5b0d-956a-44e9c4ffd06e" :answer-field/key "The function is not continuous on any of the given intervals" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668930}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d16a77c7-8df1-5b6e-bc46-f6c511c4b268" :question/math-academy-id "q-76210" :question/problem "![](images/5e/5e787dda0cccdafaa6a93176daea5f954b1cd1da0beaff410a6563536459208e.png)\n\nConsider the function $y=f(x)$ above. On which of the following intervals is the function continuous? \n\nYou may assume that all points of discontinuity of $f(x)$ are shown in the diagram.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement.\n\n- The function is continuous on $(-\\infty ,-1].$ It is continuous on $(-\\infty ,-1)$ and also left continuous at $x=-1.$\n\n- The function is *not* continuous on $[-2,0]$ because it contains a discontinuity at $x=-1.$\n\n- The function is *not* continuous on $[-1,\\infty ).$ Although the function is continuous on $(-1,\\infty ),$ it is not right-continuous at $x=-1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345197 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078487 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f00fd821-a5d4-5844-9db5-795b9e321b94" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Largest Intervals of Continuity of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa6c3498-eb14-5dde-bc00-32895a0a1c8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468184} {:answer/id #uuid "b3ab858a-b374-5436-aa52-f16a70544fa7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468185}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa6c3498-eb14-5dde-bc00-32895a0a1c8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468184} :answer-field/id #uuid "560850d5-77fd-5d0a-b265-2a9a9e2adbe2" :answer-field/key "$x\\in (-\\infty ,3]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468813} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf93c79b-db04-505a-8cb9-af0413d93bae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468186} {:answer/id #uuid "3a4e810f-2079-515b-84d8-fc8ff0b8c91a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468187}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf93c79b-db04-505a-8cb9-af0413d93bae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468186} :answer-field/id #uuid "365d22f0-a8be-5e85-bed9-0d07bbce2ca0" :answer-field/key "$x\\in (-\\infty ,5)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468814} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8be3842b-6fe6-585d-999b-97b25da90dcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468188} {:answer/id #uuid "12bceb91-74c2-5e73-9356-37da01924e13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468189}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12bceb91-74c2-5e73-9356-37da01924e13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468189} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0ef2716-8518-50cd-b34e-ca5d64fce6a3" :answer-field/key "$x\\in (4,6)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468815} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63bf2096-1ef1-5e68-9dc6-8fc7054b49ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668707} {:answer/id #uuid "b66a7a61-f630-5782-ae33-bec5962cdaad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668708}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63bf2096-1ef1-5e68-9dc6-8fc7054b49ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668707} :answer-field/id #uuid "07996b77-018a-5238-9b94-8cbed24c2d5a" :answer-field/key "The function is not continuous on any of the given intervals" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668931}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a8275053-44d7-522b-8662-3358231e9c18" :question/math-academy-id "q-76218" :question/problem "![](images/18/186ac941080da34b7c149534a2e255852241b28855c0ef15db2beee2d692007a.png)\n\nConsider the function $y=f(x)$ above. On which of the following intervals is the function continuous? \n\nYou may assume that all points of discontinuity of $f(x)$ are shown in the diagram.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement.\n\n- The function is *not* continuous on $(-\\infty ,3].$ Although the function is continuous on $(-\\infty ,3),$ it is not left-continuous at $x=3.$\n\n- The function is *not* continuous on $(-\\infty ,5)$ because it contains a discontinuity at $x=3.$\n\n- The function is continuous on $(4,6).$ It is continuous on $[3,\\infty )$ and this contains the interval $(4,6).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x\\in (4,6)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345308 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119931 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6a3d254-c96f-5aa0-9db6-a587eb7cb2de" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Expression Involving Given Determinants and Matrix Types"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65947b6c-82b4-5991-b973-67befea81244" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468208} {:answer/id #uuid "805dda68-7ce8-5f0c-839b-d424cf3215d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468209}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65947b6c-82b4-5991-b973-67befea81244" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468208} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfc3b66d-8af1-5478-a51d-5cdeb04ff05b" :answer-field/key "$-2\\text{det}({A}^{T})-3\\text{det}(I)=7$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468825} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f5517a69-aa85-583a-ae0c-57b3675d3489" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468210} {:answer/id #uuid "668fd471-d81b-5768-83b4-27ac0bda2ba4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468211}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5517a69-aa85-583a-ae0c-57b3675d3489" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468210} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ad968c4-d57c-568e-9e45-214524448f5a" :answer-field/key "$4\\text{det}({A}^{T})=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468826} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "309fbf87-4ba8-53d2-817b-acc36f8fa084" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468212} {:answer/id #uuid "8ae348c2-2cbe-582f-a32d-54ba83ae7249" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468213}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "309fbf87-4ba8-53d2-817b-acc36f8fa084" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468212} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e465ba1-1436-5630-9eb8-4db7583b91bf" :answer-field/key "$\\text{det}({A}^{T})-\\text{det}(I)=-\\frac{1}{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468827} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "052e310f-b8e2-5586-9f27-7c56bf57deb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668709} {:answer/id #uuid "bfb92a79-150d-58c5-b1ad-2f5e7c2b61bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668710}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bfb92a79-150d-58c5-b1ad-2f5e7c2b61bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668710} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3e5cedf-afce-56e3-b3df-3539941eedab" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668932}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "49749c9e-4840-5ef3-a87f-c1ce7810b100" :question/math-academy-id "q-77503" :question/problem "Given that $det(A)=2$, which of the following statements are true? \n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "From the properties of determinants, we know that \n\n$$\n\\text{det}({A}^{T})=\\text{det}(A)=2\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\ndet(I)=1.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $-2\\text{det}({A}^{T})-3\\text{det}(I)=7$ is false. We have,\n\n$$\n-2\\text{det}({A}^{T})-3\\text{det}(I)=-2\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 1=-7\\ne 7.\n$$\n\n- Statement $4\\text{det}({A}^{T})=2$ is false. We have\n\n$$\n4\\text{det}({A}^{T})=4\\cdot 2=8\\ne 2.\n$$\n\n- Statement $\\text{det}({A}^{T})-\\text{det}(I)=-\\frac{1}{2}$ is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\text{det}({A}^{T})-\\text{det}(I)=2-1=1\\ne -\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"None.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348154 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184151 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "437c168a-6799-5d13-bd9b-031290a84da6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intervals of Concavity of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4da3a19c-bae7-5f63-a92a-8aa2edb12e6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468226} {:answer/id #uuid "15a8ee57-8581-51f7-affe-d87ddfbf508c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4da3a19c-bae7-5f63-a92a-8aa2edb12e6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468226} :answer-field/id #uuid "44b5749e-c13c-50fb-93b9-69de4485ab3c" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ is concave down on $(2,\\infty )$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468834} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4eb762ba-786d-5da5-837f-acc4923ee13b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" 