ect {:answer/id #uuid "77b7d58f-0e4e-5e7d-aed4-08c91f06adcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469301} :answer-field/id #uuid "790adcf9-f3da-50a3-aa5c-dce48917f693" :answer-field/key "$T$ is a linear transformation" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470262} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ae23ec1-0e56-5576-88dc-fc0e73f4fb2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668723} {:answer/id #uuid "6997e38c-e047-512e-8868-0fa5262df2f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668724}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ae23ec1-0e56-5576-88dc-fc0e73f4fb2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668723} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d0acd58-95c6-561e-b841-63552493d6a7" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668939}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5104f251-39bc-5c29-bbcf-96e73f6b8fe5" :question/math-academy-id "q-8297" :question/problem "Let \n$T:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}3y \\\\ 2x\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A linear transformation $T$ satisfies two properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & T\\begin{bmatrix}kx \\\\ ky\\end{bmatrix}=kT\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}, \\\\  & T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the first condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\begin{bmatrix}kx \\\\ ky\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3ky \\\\ 2kx\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =k\\begin{bmatrix}3y \\\\ 2x\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =kT\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the second condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3({y}_{1}+{y}_{2}) \\\\ 2({x}_{1}+{x}_{2})\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3{y}_{1} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3{y}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{T}$ is a linear transformation.\n\nAs a result, all three statements are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354339 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133951 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "da20ffe7-173b-5fc0-8629-3b9b70222860" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Orthogonal Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e4e358b5-97fa-5dc0-9ec4-19466342da0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469410} {:answer/id #uuid "6b93d7f8-3a76-5294-8c4b-a64beffd4684" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469411}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4e358b5-97fa-5dc0-9ec4-19466342da0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469410} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a1473c4-f58e-5b7d-8f68-b11f5d273326" :answer-field/key "$3Q$ is orthogonal" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470317} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "041c92fd-b654-5bac-8d90-25928f746218" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469412} {:answer/id #uuid "2d632d7e-d7b3-5411-87cd-979fb2168d8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469413}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "041c92fd-b654-5bac-8d90-25928f746218" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469412} :answer-field/id #uuid "577e09cf-386e-5aa7-97ec-f5672711e8a1" :answer-field/key "${Q}^{T}$ is **not** orthogonal" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470318} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cfb7808c-9349-508d-be48-6a448e81e286" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469414} {:answer/id #uuid "2e2826a9-8fd1-543d-8c80-03ed36d83923" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469415}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cfb7808c-9349-508d-be48-6a448e81e286" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469414} :answer-field/id #uuid "fefed51c-a546-5c98-b8b5-becce51ddb02" :answer-field/key "${Q}^{5}$ is the zero matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470319} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "927f8022-705c-5271-bda0-b8c3b10e7eb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668725} {:answer/id #uuid "0644fcb8-b24d-52a8-9559-b1cc945aa919" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668726}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0644fcb8-b24d-52a8-9559-b1cc945aa919" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668726} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bc6a081-8853-5e38-a9f7-5d683643b1e4" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668940}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "27c490dd-1808-531c-8cd0-cdd298d3c924" :question/math-academy-id "q-84786" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the orthogonal matrix $Q?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a matrix $Q$ is orthogonal if and only if\n\n$$\nQ{Q}^{T}={Q}^{T}Q=I.\n$$\n\nTo check that a matrix is orthogonal, it is sufficient to check that the above equation is satisfied.\n\nMoreover, we have the following properties:\n\n- For any orthogonal matrix $Q,$ we have ${Q}^{-1}={Q}^{T}.$\n\n- $(AB)^{T}={B}^{T}{A}^{T}$ for conformable matrices $A$ and $B.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “$3Q$ is orthogonal” is false. Computing the product $3Q\\cdot (3Q)^{T},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3Q\\cdot (3Q)^{T} & =3Q\\cdot 3{Q}^{T} \\\\  & =9Q{Q}^{T} \\\\  & =9I \\\\  & \\ne I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${Q}^{T}$ is **not** orthogonal” is false. Computing the product ${Q}^{T}\\cdot ({Q}^{T})^{T},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Q}^{T}\\cdot ({Q}^{T})^{T} & ={Q}^{T}Q \\\\  & =I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${Q}^{5}$ is the zero matrix” is false. Let's consider the identity matrix\n\n$$\nQ=I=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWe have that $Q$ is an orthogonal matrix and also ${Q}^{5}=Q\\ne O.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354532 :knowledge-poin